Id: stor004w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
References: cryptsetup(8)
Controls: CIS 3.6, 3.11; NIST SC-28; ISO 8.24

This machine has a battery of its own (a laptop or a tablet), so it
can be lost or stolen, and some of its local file systems are not
encrypted (the detail lists them). Whoever has the machine can then
read everything on those disks, the user's files and any keys and
passwords stored there, by booting something else or taking the disk
out. A battery of a connected device (a wireless mouse) does not
count.

To fix it, encrypt them with LUKS: every distribution's installer
offers it, and 'cryptsetup reencrypt' converts an existing partition in
place (after a backup). The boot partition can stay as it is.
